# Thread 3 — 💡 SUGGESTION: escalation packet lists demotions for resolved identities too

**Fixed.** `demotionRecords` now filters to open statuses — the first of the two suggested options, matching the existing render contract.

## What changed

`js/common/findingRegistry.js`:

```javascript
function demotionRecords(items) {
    return items.filter(function(i) {
        return !!i.demotion && isOpenStatus(i.status);
    }).map(...);
}
```

- A demoted identity that was later **fixed** or **withdrawn** no longer appears in `buildEscalationPacket(registry).demotions`, so `buildEscalationPacketComment` stops rendering `⚠️ F3 (src/auth.ts) demoted from BLOCKING — ... (a cited re-raise re-elevates it)` for items the instruction no longer applies to.
- This is the same open-status dedup space (`isOpenStatus` = `open` | `re-introduced`) `buildFindingsInjection` already renders its demotion guidance from — the two renders agree by construction now.
- The structured record still carries `status` (harmless, self-describing for consumers).

## Tests (RED first — 3 failed on the pre-fix head)

New suite `gh-1334 — escalation packet lists demotions of open identities only (rework)` in `js/unit-tests/test_findingRegistry.js`:

- a demotion later **fixed** leaves `packet.demotions` and the rendered comment (the comment itself still renders — rounds exist);
- a demotion later **withdrawn** likewise leaves both;
- an open demotion registered alongside a resolved one still surfaces with its provenance (`n`, `status: 'open'`, `claimMatchedTicket: inconclusive`) and the resolved F-label is not rendered;
- `buildFindingsInjection` keeps its open-only guidance contract (unchanged, pinned).

# Thread 4 — 💡 SUGGESTION: `registryClaimOf` truncates reviewer claims that legitimately contain a `---` horizontal rule

**Fixed.** The strip now cuts only at the known machine tail — precise and loss-free, exactly as suggested.

## What changed

- `js/common/reviewSpecClaims.js` — the demotion tail's head is now the exported constant `DEMOTION_NOTE_HEAD` (`'---\n⚠️ **Severity demoted'`), and `downgradeNote` composes from it, so the cut point can never drift from the produced annotation.
- `js/postPRReviewComments.js`:

```javascript
var DEMOTION_TAIL_SEPARATOR = '\n' + reviewSpecClaims.DEMOTION_NOTE_HEAD;

function registryClaimOf(claim) {
    var text = String(claim || '');
    var cut = text.indexOf(DEMOTION_TAIL_SEPARATOR);
    return cut === -1 ? text : text.substring(0, cut);
}
```

The generic `split('\n---\n')` is gone: a reviewer-authored multi-paragraph claim containing a markdown horizontal rule keeps **everything** after the rule in the registry identity, so cross-round similarity (gh-1332 dedup) runs on the full text. Machine-appended demotion tails are still stripped completely (note + marker).

## Tests

New tests in `js/unit-tests/test_postPRReviewComments.js`:

- a claim with a legitimate `\n---\n` rule keeps its full text (both paragraphs present in `findingsFromReviewData(...)[0].claim`);
- the machine tail is cut exactly — the registry claim is *exactly* the reviewer text (no separator, no confirm-note, no `dmtools:demoted-from-BLOCKING` marker), with the structured `demotion` provenance still riding along (the existing provenance test continues to pass).

